      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقْعَدُ</span></b>  A camel <i>having a laxness and depression
in the shank.</i> See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَعَدٌ</span>. (TA.) But see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصْدَفَ</span> ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ أَقْعَدُ مِنْ فُلَانٍ</span> (tropical:)  <i>Such a one is more
nearly related to his chief,</i> or <i>oldest, ancestor
than such a one.</i> (IAar, IAth, L.) See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُعْدُدٌ</span>.

